From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SurfaceFlinger: physical displays use the default composition format

Build 069 (QEMU ARM32 ATV, emulation only): virtio-gpu in Linux 6.6 accepts only
XRGB8888/ARGB8888 KMS framebuffers (virtgpu_display.c) and its dumb buffers are
created as XRGB8888. processDisplayAdded() hard-codes RGBA_8888 (DRM ABGR8888)
for the client target of physical displays, so drm_hwcomposer could never
create a framebuffer ("could not create drm fb -2", BAD_LAYER) and no frame was
shown. Use ro.surface_flinger.default_composition_pixel_format (default
RGBA_8888, so behaviour is unchanged unless the property is set).
---
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -3817,7 +3817,9 @@
     ui::PixelFormat pixelFormat = static_cast<ui::PixelFormat>(PIXEL_FORMAT_UNKNOWN);
     if (state.physical) {
         resolution = state.physical->activeMode->getResolution();
-        pixelFormat = static_cast<ui::PixelFormat>(PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBA_8888);
+        // Build 069: honour ro.surface_flinger.default_composition_pixel_format
+        // (RGBA_8888 unless set), e.g. BGRA_8888 for virtio-gpu scanout.
+        pixelFormat = defaultCompositionPixelFormat;
     } else if (state.surface != nullptr) {
         int status = state.surface->query(NATIVE_WINDOW_WIDTH, &resolution.width);
         ALOGE_IF(status != NO_ERROR, "Unable to query width (%d)", status);
